hadith for Debian
-----------------

The cookie files are built at package build time from corpus/*.jsonl by
tools/make_fortune.py, and are not shipped ready-made in the source. Running
the pipeline (parse -> qa -> modernise -> make_fortune) is what produces those
JSONL files in the first place; the package build only renders them.

Both corpora are installed as ordinary fortune cookie files:

    /usr/share/games/fortunes/hadith-suhrawardy        the modernised text
    /usr/share/games/fortunes/hadith-suhrawardy-1905   the 1905 wording

so `fortune` on its own will draw from them along with every other installed
cookie file. The `hadith` command exists to draw from these two alone, and to
make the modernised text the default.

The (saw) after the Prophet's name is added when the cookie files are
rendered, not in either corpus. See hadith(6), NOTES.

 -- Masroor Ahmad <debian@masroor.de>, Sat, 01 Aug 2026 16:26:46 +0200
